<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:folio="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/bpmn" xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  id="Definitions_CodeChangeReview"
                  targetNamespace="https://folio-assistant.dev/workflows"
                  exporter="folio-assistant" exporterVersion="0.1.0">

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       A change to the PLATFORM, from claimed work item to merged.

       Bean `folio-assistant-haya` step 2, issue #363. The audit in
       `fsh-guts/proposals/sdlc-process-audit.md` found that
       `content-change-review.bpmn` models this exact loop at 22
       activities, with a CI/CD lane — for CONTENT. There was no
       code-change sibling, which is why the audit scored INTEGRATION and
       VERIFICATION as unowned: not for want of vocabulary, roles or
       skills, but because the one diagram that draws them takes a
       content change as its subject.

       This is that sibling. It CALLS the subprocesses that already exist
       rather than restating them — `prepare-merge`, `watch`,
       `review-code` — because a second description of a process is a
       second thing free to disagree with the first.

       DELIBERATELY NO DEPLOYMENT LANE. The audit's row 7 is the one row
       whose activities differ per topology, so it waits on the axes
       being not merely agreed but exercised. Everything here is
       topology-independent: an agent commits, gates run, a reviewer
       reads, a branch merges, wherever it is deployed afterwards.
       Owner's default on #363, 2026-09-19.
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_CodeChangeReview">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_CodeChangeReview" name="Platform change — claim to merge" processRef="Process_CodeChangeReview" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>

  <bpmn:process id="Process_CodeChangeReview" name="Code change and review" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Getting a change to the PLATFORM from "this is needed" to merged: claim the work, branch and announce it, make the change, prove it against the platform's own gates, and carry it through review to a merge somebody else is not left holding.

You are in this process for a change to folio-assistant itself. `content-change-review` is the same shape for a folio's content, and the acceptance differs: here a code reviewer judges the engineering, there a review committee judges the editorial.

The loop back through "root-cause the failure" is the point of drawing this at all. Red CI is not a state you report and leave; it is a state you re-enter the process from. The same is true of a review that is not clear.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <!-- STRICT, and declared rather than defaulted. `process-model.ts`
           treats an absent policy as strict, so 16 of the 33 diagrams here
           are strict because nobody typed the attribute (bean
           `folio-assistant-30hn`). This one says so on purpose: the steps
           it gates are the ones agents skip under time pressure —
           running the gates, and opening the PR at the first commit. -->
      <folio:policy enforcement="strict" />
      <!-- Capture ON. This process ends in a write to `main`, so what ran
           before that write is exactly the audit question. Same reasoning
           as `content-lifecycle`. -->
      <folio:log capture="on" />
      <!-- PROCESS-SCOPED CONVENTION (bean `3190`). Every step in this diagram
           writes or reviews code, so the comment convention holds throughout
           and is bound once here rather than restated on nine activities.
           Bound at the PROCESS rather than globally on purpose: an agent
           adjudicating a translation is not in this diagram and does not get
           it, which is the whole distinction — "absent binding means NO
           conventions, not all of them". -->
      <folio:convention ref="comment-why-not-what" />
    </bpmn:extensionElements>

    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_CodeChangeReview">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Agent" name="Authoring agent">
        <bpmn:documentation>The `no-clean-run-over-an-empty-set` convention is bound at this lane specifically because this is the one lane that writes checks — Lane_Pipeline runs them and Lane_Reviewer reads someone else's, so a check with nothing to assert over is this lane's failure mode to guard against, nobody else's. Every activity that is not mechanical execution (Lane_Pipeline) or an outside judgement (Lane_Reviewer) sits here, including both loop-backs — a red gate returns to Task_Implement through Task_Diagnose, and review findings return to it through Task_AddressReview — so this lane never hands work off without also owning what comes back.</bpmn:documentation>
        <!-- Bound EXPLICITLY rather than by lane name. `roles.json` matches a
             lane to a role by its name, and that role already carries five
             aliases because five diagrams each named this lane differently —
             the alias list is the problem accumulating, not the solution. This
             diagram's own near-miss makes the case: "CI/CD pipeline" below
             differs from the declared "CI/CD Pipeline" by one capital letter,
             which no reader would catch and the audit did. -->
        <bpmn:extensionElements>
          <folio:role ref="authoring-agent"/>
          <!-- LANE-SCOPED (bean `3190`), and the scope is the point. This lane
               writes the checks; the reviewer and the pipeline lanes below do
               not, so binding it here rather than on the process says who the
               rule is for. `workflow_next` reports the scope beside the ref so
               an agent can tell "every step in this process" from "this lane
               only" — two different claims that a flat list would merge. -->
          <folio:convention ref="no-clean-run-over-an-empty-set"/>
        </bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_Change</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ClaimBean</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_BranchAndAnnounce</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Implement</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_RunGates</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_CommitAndOpenPR</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_CIGreen</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Diagnose</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_ReviewClear</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_AddressReview</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_PrepareMerge</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_CloseBean</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Merged</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Pipeline" name="CI/CD pipeline">
        <bpmn:documentation>Exists as a separate lane for one reason: what it tests — the merge of head into base — is not a claim the Agent lane could make about its own tree, so GW_CIGreen has to be fed by an independent run rather than by the agent reporting its own gates as done.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements><folio:role ref="build-pipeline"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_RunCI</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Reviewer" name="Code reviewer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Its verdict, not the agent's own account of the diff, is what GW_ReviewClear reads: a finding routes the change back through Task_AddressReview to Task_Implement, and only a clear routes it forward to Task_PrepareMerge, so this lane alone determines which of those two paths a change takes.</bpmn:documentation>
        <!-- This one DOES match by name, and is still bound explicitly: a
             binding that works by coincidence of wording is one rename from
             silently unbinding. -->
        <bpmn:extensionElements><folio:role ref="code-reviewer"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Review</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>

    <!-- ═══ Agent lane ═══ -->

    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_Change" name="A platform change is needed">
      <bpmn:outgoing>f1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_ClaimBean" name="Claim the work item">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        Claim before you work. A claim ANNOUNCES rather than reserves until
        the PR exists, which is why the branch is announced at the next
        step and not at the end.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="bean-coordination"/>
        <folio:bean op="claim"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>f1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_BranchAndAnnounce" name="Branch, and announce it">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        Announce the branch WHEN IT IS CREATED, not when the work is done.
        The gap between one agent's view of an issue and everyone else's is
        what this closes.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="issue-working"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>f2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_Implement" name="Make the change">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        The loop's only open-ended step. Everything around it is procedure;
        this is the work.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="continual-progress"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>f3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>f11</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>f14</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_RunGates" name="Run the platform&#39;s own gates">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        Before pushing, not after CI says so. `bun test` passing is NOT the
        gates passing: measured 2026-09-19, a green unit suite sat beside a
        `tsc` failure and a missing `@graphNode` tag, and the second broke
        a QA sidecar comparison as well — one cause, two symptoms, and an
        agent running only the tests would have pushed all three.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <!-- This activity carried a `<folio:no-skill>` exemption when the
             diagram landed: the SDLC audit had found that nothing told an
             agent to run the platform's own gates, and the exemption WAS
             the Verification phase being unowned, recorded rather than
             papered over. Bean `folio-assistant-n60j` closed it. -->
        <folio:skill ref="platform-gates"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>f4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_CommitAndOpenPR" name="Commit, push, open the PR">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        The PR opens at the FIRST commit, even on a stub, and permission is
        never asked for it. Holding a green PR back for someone to look at
        is not caution — it is a blocked reviewer.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="continual-progress"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>f5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_CIGreen" name="CI green?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Answered by the gates run against the merge of head into base. `green` goes to review; `red` goes to root-causing the failure first, since a red change is never waiting on review.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>f7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f8</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_Diagnose" name="Root-cause the failure">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        "Flake" is not a root cause. A red PR is work now, whatever its
        review state — only a green, mergeable head waits on reviewers.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="ci-health"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>f9</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f11</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_ReviewClear" name="Review clear?">
      <bpmn:documentation>The reviewer's result. `findings` go back to be addressed; `clear` goes to preparing the merge and watching it through.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>f12</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f13</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f15</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_AddressReview" name="Address the review">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        Every finding is answered — implemented, or replied to with why
        not. A design question does not excuse skipping the nits in the
        same review.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <!-- `watch`, NOT `code-node-review`. That skill's own front matter
             says `roles: [code-reviewer, admin]` — it is the reviewer's
             instrument, and binding it here would have the agent reviewing
             its own change. What the agent needs is the follow-through
             discipline: answer every finding or say why not, and keep the PR
             moving until it is merged or closed. -->
        <folio:skill ref="watch"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>f13</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f14</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_PrepareMerge" name="Prepare the merge, and watch it through">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        `prepare-merge` brings the base in, re-runs the gates and pushes —
        it does NOT merge. `watch` follows the PR until it is merged or
        closed, because webhooks do not reliably deliver CI success or a
        merge-conflict transition.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="prepare-merge"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>f15</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f16</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_CloseBean" name="Record what was done, and close">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        A closed work item is read later by somebody deciding whether to
        reopen the subject, so "completed" with nothing behind it cannot be
        audited. An ISSUE is never closed on the agent's own say-so.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="todo-manager"/>
        <folio:bean op="resolve"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>f16</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f17</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Merged" name="Merged">
      <bpmn:incoming>f17</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>

    <!-- ═══ Pipeline lane ═══ -->

    <bpmn:task id="Task_RunCI" name="Run the gates against the merge of head into base">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        CI tests the MERGE, not the branch. That is why a locally green
        tree can go red here: the agent's tree and the merge result are
        different trees, and the difference is invisible from a checkout.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:no-skill reason="A mechanical actor runs this — GitHub Actions executes the workflow. There is no instruction body for an agent to follow, and a skill here would describe somebody else's behaviour."/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>f6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>

    <!-- ═══ Reviewer lane ═══ -->

    <bpmn:task id="Task_Review" name="Review the change">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        A human or an agent acting AS reviewer. Nothing is a reviewer;
        somebody acts as one for the duration of this lane.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="code-node-review"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>f8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f12</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>

    <!-- ═══ Sequence flows ═══ -->
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f1"  sourceRef="Start_Change"          targetRef="Task_ClaimBean" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f2"  sourceRef="Task_ClaimBean"        targetRef="Task_BranchAndAnnounce" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f3"  sourceRef="Task_BranchAndAnnounce" targetRef="Task_Implement" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f4"  sourceRef="Task_Implement"        targetRef="Task_RunGates" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f5"  sourceRef="Task_RunGates"         targetRef="Task_CommitAndOpenPR" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f6"  sourceRef="Task_CommitAndOpenPR"  targetRef="Task_RunCI" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f7"  sourceRef="Task_RunCI"            targetRef="GW_CIGreen" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f8"  name="green"     sourceRef="GW_CIGreen"     targetRef="Task_Review" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f9"  name="red"       sourceRef="GW_CIGreen"     targetRef="Task_Diagnose" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f11" sourceRef="Task_Diagnose"         targetRef="Task_Implement" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f12" sourceRef="Task_Review"           targetRef="GW_ReviewClear" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f13" name="findings"  sourceRef="GW_ReviewClear" targetRef="Task_AddressReview" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f14" sourceRef="Task_AddressReview"    targetRef="Task_Implement" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f15" name="clear"     sourceRef="GW_ReviewClear" targetRef="Task_PrepareMerge" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f16" sourceRef="Task_PrepareMerge"     targetRef="Task_CloseBean" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f17" sourceRef="Task_CloseBean"        targetRef="End_Merged" />
  </bpmn:process>

  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_CodeChangeReview">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_CodeChangeReview" bpmnElement="Collaboration_CodeChangeReview">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Participant_CodeChangeReview" bpmnElement="Participant_CodeChangeReview" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1700" height="520" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Agent" bpmnElement="Lane_Agent" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="190" y="80" width="1670" height="300" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Pipeline" bpmnElement="Lane_Pipeline" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="190" y="380" width="1670" height="110" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Reviewer" bpmnElement="Lane_Reviewer" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="190" y="490" width="1670" height="110" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>

      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Start_Change" bpmnElement="Start_Change">
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="226" y="196" width="80" height="27" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
        <dc:Bounds x="240" y="152" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_ClaimBean" bpmnElement="Task_ClaimBean">
        <dc:Bounds x="330" y="130" width="140" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_BranchAndAnnounce" bpmnElement="Task_BranchAndAnnounce">
        <dc:Bounds x="520" y="130" width="140" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Implement" bpmnElement="Task_Implement">
        <dc:Bounds x="710" y="130" width="140" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_RunGates" bpmnElement="Task_RunGates">
        <dc:Bounds x="900" y="130" width="140" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_CommitAndOpenPR" bpmnElement="Task_CommitAndOpenPR">
        <dc:Bounds x="1090" y="130" width="140" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_GW_CIGreen" bpmnElement="GW_CIGreen" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1290" y="112" width="60" height="14" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
        <dc:Bounds x="1295" y="145" width="50" height="50" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Diagnose" bpmnElement="Task_Diagnose">
        <dc:Bounds x="1250" y="250" width="140" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_GW_ReviewClear" bpmnElement="GW_ReviewClear" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1435" y="112" width="70" height="14" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
        <dc:Bounds x="1445" y="145" width="50" height="50" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_AddressReview" bpmnElement="Task_AddressReview">
        <dc:Bounds x="1400" y="250" width="140" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_PrepareMerge" bpmnElement="Task_PrepareMerge">
        <dc:Bounds x="1550" y="130" width="140" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_CloseBean" bpmnElement="Task_CloseBean">
        <dc:Bounds x="1550" y="250" width="140" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_End_Merged" bpmnElement="End_Merged">
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1784" y="326" width="48" height="14" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
        <dc:Bounds x="1770" y="272" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>

      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_RunCI" bpmnElement="Task_RunCI">
        <dc:Bounds x="1090" y="395" width="180" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Review" bpmnElement="Task_Review">
        <dc:Bounds x="1320" y="505" width="140" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>

      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_f1" bpmnElement="f1">
        <di:waypoint x="276" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="330" y="170" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_f2" bpmnElement="f2">
        <di:waypoint x="470" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="520" y="170" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_f3" bpmnElement="f3">
        <di:waypoint x="660" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="710" y="170" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_f4" bpmnElement="f4">
        <di:waypoint x="850" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="900" y="170" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_f5" bpmnElement="f5">
        <di:waypoint x="1040" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="1090" y="170" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_f6" bpmnElement="f6">
        <di:waypoint x="1160" y="210" /><di:waypoint x="1160" y="395" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_f7" bpmnElement="f7">
        <di:waypoint x="1270" y="435" /><di:waypoint x="1320" y="435" /><di:waypoint x="1320" y="170" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_f8" bpmnElement="f8">
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1330" y="330" width="40" height="14" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
        <di:waypoint x="1345" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="1390" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="1390" y="545" /><di:waypoint x="1320" y="545" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_f9" bpmnElement="f9">
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1300" y="212" width="30" height="14" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
